lication process, value and duration of these awards and scholarships differ.\nAdmission Funding Offer\nA funding offer, outlining various sources of funding, may have been outlined in your admission offer when you applied for admission to your graduate program. Be sure to read the sections of the Graduate Student Handbook on Admission Funding Offer to understand the sources and rules of your funding offer.\nApply for Awards\nThe Student Document Library provides a range of samples and templates, including Outline of Proposed Studies, Thesis Completion Timeline etc.\nMost internal and donor awards are applied for in the GA3 Awards System.\nPro Tip: Watch the GA3 walk-through video to help guide you through using GA3\nApply now through GA3\nInternal + Donor Funded Awards\nInternal and Donor Funded awards are funded through the University\u2019s Scholarship, Bursary and Award funds, Departmental or Faculty funds or through the generosity of our donors.\nLearn More\nTri-agency & Government Awards\nTri-agency & Government Awards are funded through private, provincial or federal sources.\nLearn More\nExternal + Additional Awards\nThis page lists external funding agencies, organized by research areas or funding audience.\nLearn More\nRoles + Responsibilities\nKnow your roles and responsibilities throughout the award process.\nLearn More\nPayments + Policies\nDetails on how your awards are paid out and how to manage your award.\nLearn More\nUndergraduate Student Research Awards\nThe USRA program is funded through various sources and is designated for undergraduate students looking for graduate level research experience.\nLearn More\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nAbout\nApply\nAwards + Funding\nGraduate Students\nLife + Community\nContact us\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nMaggie Benston Centre 1100\nSimon Fraser University\n8888 University Drive\nBurnaby, B.C.\nCanada V5A 1S6\nSafety & Risk\nSFU Maps & Directions\nSFU Admissions\nRoad Report\nGive to SFU\nEmergency Informatio